# Phase 6 demo requests (docs/plans/phase-6.md). Most of Phase 6 is the web portal: open http://localhost:8090
# (or https://<laptop-ip>:8443 with the lan profile, README "Phone demo"). These are the API changes behind it.
# Run with the VS Code REST Client or IntelliJ's HTTP client, top to bottom.

@gw = http://localhost:8080

### --- log in ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# @name organizer
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "organizer.a@mitpass.test", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

###
# @name organizerB
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "organizer.b@mitpass.test", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

###
# @name admin
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "admin@mitpass.test", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

###
# @name priya
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "2026509001@student.annauniv.edu", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

### --- 1. Automatic refresh: what the portal does when the access token is about to expire -------------------------

### 200 New access + refresh token; the old refresh token is spent (rotation, D7)
# @name refreshed
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{priya.response.body.refreshToken}}"}

### 401 refresh-token-reused: the same old token again ends the whole login. The portal's per-session lock
### (docs/plans/phase-6.md §7) makes sure parallel page requests never do this.
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{priya.response.body.refreshToken}}"}

### --- 2. Draft events are private to their organizer and admins (owner decision Q12, D15) ------------------------

### 201 A new event starts as DRAFT
# @name draft
POST {{gw}}/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "DRAFTDEMO1", "title": "Draft demo", "categoryId": 1, "venueId": 1, "capacity": 10,
 "startsAt": "2099-12-14T03:30:00Z", "endsAt": "2099-12-14T09:30:00Z",
 "registrationOpensAt": "2099-11-01T03:30:00Z", "registrationClosesAt": "2099-12-13T12:30:00Z",
 "eligibleDepartments": [], "minYear": null, "maxYear": null}

### 404 for anyone else (no token)
GET {{gw}}/api/events/{{draft.response.body.id}}

### 404 for another organizer
GET {{gw}}/api/events/{{draft.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerB.response.body.accessToken}}

### 200 for its organizer; the catalogue lists it only for them and admins
GET {{gw}}/api/events/{{draft.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}

### 200 The organizer's list carries allowedTransitions per event (one call for "My events", D9 row)
GET {{gw}}/api/events?organizerId=00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002&size=100
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}

### --- 3. The verification link now opens the portal ------------------------------------------------------------

### Sign up, then open Mailpit (http://localhost:8025): the link is http://localhost:8090/verify-email?token=…
### The portal page shows a button; pressing it sends this (the GET alone spends nothing):
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{"token": "paste-the-token-from-the-email"}

### --- 4. Admin: system health through the gateway (owner decision Q3, D15) ---------------------------------------

### 200 Every registered instance with status and component names; one that doesn't answer in 2 s is DOWN
GET {{gw}}/api/admin/health
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 403 problem forbidden: ADMIN only (the gateway owns this one rule)
GET {{gw}}/api/admin/health
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}

### 401 without a token
GET {{gw}}/api/admin/health

### --- 5. The pass card's QR as SVG (endpoint from Phase 4; the portal now passes it through, crisp at any size) ---

### 200 image/svg+xml (or 409 code-locked before the code unlocks 2 h before doors open)
# @name passes
GET {{gw}}/api/passes/me
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}

###
GET {{gw}}/api/passes/{{passes.response.body.content[0].id}}/qr/live?format=svg
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}
